# Attachment upload = upload relay + browser-specific body shape

## Relays (like relay.encrypt.lu)

| Environment | App host | Upload origin |
|---|---|---|
| Production | `privatenote.ai` | `https://upload.privatenote.ai` |
| Staging (same-site) | `premium.privatenote.ai` | `https://upload-staging.privatenote.ai` |

Resolved by `uploadWorkerOriginForAppHostname()` / `isStagingAppHost()`.

## Browser policy

| Browser | Encrypt | HTTP |
|---|---|---|
| Chrome / Firefox | one secretstream frame (`totalChunks = 1`) | one `PUT /file` Blob |
| Safari | ~1 MiB secretstream frames | sequential `POST /file/chunks/:i` (~1 MiB bodies, headerless, token in query) |

Safari drops multi‑MiB single XHRs (`status: 0` / “network connection was lost”) even on same-site `premium.privatenote.ai` → `upload-staging.privatenote.ai`. Do **not** force Safari onto single-Blob.

Never point Safari binary uploads at `*.workers.dev` for large bodies.
Prefer same-site SPA hosts for QA (`privatenote.ai` / `premium.privatenote.ai`), not `*.pages.dev`.
